<title>ARGENTINA: Menem urges Chirac to halt farm subsidies.</title>
<headline>Menem urges Chirac to halt farm subsidies.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine President Carlos Menem Monday urged his French counterpart Jacques Chirac to put an end to farm subsidies hurting Argentine grain exports.</p>
<p>In a speech at the Buenos Aires stock exchange on the first full day of Chirac's state visit, Menem hailed the excellent state of bilateral relations.</p>
<p>But he added: &quot;We must overcome the issues pertaining to agriculture.&quot;</p>
<p>Argentina is a major producer of wheat and other grains and has traditionally complained about European Union and U.S. farm subsidies.</p>
<p>Menem also asked Chirac to help Argentina access the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD), a Paris-based group of countries.</p>
<p>&quot;We are capable of joining due to our (economic) transformation process which has evidently become an example for other countries that are lagging behind&quot; in trade liberalization and market deregulation, he said.</p>
<p>((--David Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0652))</p>
